    {
      "src": "II:1",
      "role": "model",
      "mode": "typed",
      "prompt": "If we want to evaluate a sum, like this one…  2/6 + 3/6  …that means we want to say the value of the fraction. It’s not enough to write it as a single fraction, like this:  (2 + 3)/6",
      "expected": "5/6",
      "demo": "It isn’t evaluated – we can’t say the value – until there’s just one number on top and bottom, like this: *5/6*."
    },
    {
      "src": "II:8",
      "role": "model",
      "mode": "typed",
      "prompt": "And so if I wanted to evaluate this expression:  5/6 + 3/6  First I would write it as a single fraction:",
      "expected": "(5 + 3)/6",
      "demo": "*(5 + 3)/6*."
    },
    {
      "src": "II:12",
      "role": "model",
      "mode": "frac",
      "prompt": "And then evaluate:",
      "expr": "(5 + 3)/6 =",
      "frac": { "num": null, "den": null },
      "expected": "8/6",
      "demo": "*8/6*."
    },
